1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,710
Chaining API calls in Arazzo?

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:04,800
Usually: YAML, by hand.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,342
Meet the Arazzo canvas,
inside the GitHub Copilot app.

4
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:11,397
Just ask, and Copilot opens your workflow.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,946
Your API operations are right there.

6
00:00:14,946 --> 00:00:19,679
Drag them onto the canvas:
each drop adds a step, saved to the file.

7
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,129
Then wire an input to a parameter.

8
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,888
Or let Copilot write the rest.

9
00:00:25,888 --> 00:00:29,434
Ask from the canvas,
about the step you selected.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,684
Copilot edits the very same canvas.

11
00:00:32,684 --> 00:00:36,770
It passes the pet id,
retries the order, and returns its id.

12
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:38,976
You watch every change land.

13
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:46,064
The result: valid Arazzo,
written to your file as you go.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,337
The Arazzo canvas for GitHub Copilot.

15
00:00:51,337 --> 00:00:53,080
Drag, wire, ask.
